1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:06,000
We audit why AI assistants don't cite a brand, and why the visitors who do arrive don't stay.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Eight skills, one entrypoint: audit-orchestrator. Python standard library only.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Our core insight: generative engine optimisation is a staged pipeline, not a ranking.

4
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:25,000
A page must clear every gate in order, and the gate it fails decides the fix.

5
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Fail at selection, and the fix is to declare the entity, not to write more content.

6
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:39,000
Our signals come from measured data: 602 prompts and 21,143 citations across three AI engines.

7
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:46,000
Only 76.44% of pages an engine had already chosen to cite could actually be fetched.

8
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:52,000
So reachability is a gate, with per-type JavaScript render-fault diagnosis.

9
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:58,000
Being cited is not the same as mattering.

10
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:04,000
Perplexity cites 2.4× more sources than ChatGPT, but absorbs each about a quarter as deeply.

11
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:10,000
So selection and absorption are audited separately, because they need different fixes.

12
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:17,000
Evidence genres (code, numbers, definitions, comparisons) measurably lift absorption.

13
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:24,000
'Add an FAQ' is standard advice, and the only genre the research measures as negative.

14
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Our marketplace never recommends it, and a regression test enforces that.

15
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:37,000
Thresholds sit at the bottom quartile: a floor to clear, not a target to chase.

16
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:45,000
Flag everything below the top quartile and you fire on most of the web. Precision first.

17
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:52,000
Severity asks how much it costs. Critical means the brand cannot enter the candidate pool.

18
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:59,000
Claim level asks how sure we are, and caps severity. A mechanism guess can never be critical.

19
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:05,000
A causal promise is never a finding; it becomes a labelled hypothesis instead.

20
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:10,000
The cap is enforced three times: at construction, in advisory review, and in schema validation.

21
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:16,000
Detectors are optimistic by design, so every finding must survive an advisory critic.

22
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:23,000
It needs a real URL and observed value, a real threshold breach, and enough sampled pages.

23
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:29,000
Weak claims are dropped or downgraded. Nothing reaches the report without passing the critic.

24
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:35,000
Three symptoms of one JavaScript render fault merge into a single root-cause fix.

25
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:41,000
Every suggested action names its mechanism and how to verify the fix.

26
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:47,000
Priority is not severity. Findings sort by severity, then pipeline order: causes first.

27
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:52,000
We prefer adding the missing fact over rewriting the page; rewrites measurably backfired.

28
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:59,600
Now live: Claude Code with Claude Opus 5.5, on a site the audit has never seen.
